# General safety net: an eprot/ checkpoint dir under any tests_rate* sweep
# results dir should always be local-only, per every sweep in this project
# (see DEVLOG.txt). Added after the refine sweep's checkpoints briefly got
# committed because the specific rule above was added one commit too late
# -- this catches any future sweep directory even if a specific line is
# forgotten again.
softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/**/eprot/

# data.dat itself is local-only from here on, same reasoning as eprot/:
# moves=300000 (the paper-matched sweep) already produces ~50-57MB
# data.dat files, over GitHub's 50MB recommended-max warning and heading
# toward its 100MB hard limit as run lengths grow further (this project's
# own direction -- the paper's own range goes up to 1e6 moves, and the
# eventual ~200-residue target will need longer runs still, not shorter).
# See DEVLOG.txt, 2026-09-30 entry. Existing SMALLER already-committed
# data.dat files (every sweep before this one, all comfortably under the
# warning threshold) are left as historical record, not retroactively
# untracked -- this only stops NEW large ones from being added.
softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/**/data.dat

# Plots (plot_run.py, plot_structural_metrics.py, identify_k_sites.py) are
# generated locally from data.dat/eprot checkpoints -- local-only for the
# same reason eprot/ itself is: regeneratable from data already gitignored,
# and PNGs would bloat the repo the same way the accidental eprot/ commit
# did. Also covers structural_metrics.csv (compute_structural_metrics.py's
# output) -- cheap to regenerate from a *.pt checkpoint set that's itself
# never committed, so keeping the CSV out too avoids a committed artifact
# whose source can't be reproduced from what's actually in the repo.
*.png
# Keep paper-scale temperature-sweep plots tracked
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/T*/
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/T*/sim0/
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/T*/sim0/plots/
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/T*/sim0/plots/*.png




softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/**/structural_metrics.csv
softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/k_sites_plots*/
!softmax/monte_carlo/protein_g*/k_sites_plots_tests_rate_sweep_temperature_paper_scale/



